@@ -9,6 +9,33 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## WebMCP
+
+The shared layout registers four client-side tools through the native
+[`document.modelContext` API](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/):
+
+| Tool | Inputs | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search_articles` | Optional `query` string | Search titles and summaries, or list all articles. Returns slugs and URLs. |
+| `get_reading_list` | None | Return saved articles in the current browser session. |
+| `set_article_bookmark` | `slug`, `saved` boolean | Save or remove an article; safe to retry with the same state. |
+| `open_article` | `slug` | Navigate the visible app to an existing article. |
+
+Use a WebMCP-enabled browser in a secure context (HTTPS or localhost). Unsupported
+browsers skip registration and retain the normal UI. No polyfill, external MCP
+server, or API key is needed. Tools use the same article search and session API
+as the UI, and bookmark changes update mounted controls and reading-list flyouts.
+The server still accepts the existing `{ slug }` toggle request, while tools and
+UI controls send explicit `{ slug, saved }` requests.
+
+Registration happens once per document, survives Astro client navigation, and is
+released by an AbortSignal during hot module replacement or registration failure.
+Execution cancellation is passed to network requests. Tools return serializable
+objects, including actionable `{ error }` results for failures and invalid input.
+
+Run `pnpm test` (Node 24+) for tool execution and registration tests, and
+`pnpm build` for the production build. No browser verification is required.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
